# Prefer tools over CLI

When a dedicated tool can do the job, use it instead of `Shell`.

## Use these instead of the terminal

| Task | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Read a file | `Read` (not `cat` / `head` / `tail`) |
| Edit a file | `StrReplace` / `Write` (not `sed` / `awk`) |
| Find files by name | `Glob` (not `find`) |
| Search file contents | `Grep` (not `rg` / `grep` in the shell) |
| Service/docs APIs | `GetMcpTools` then `CallMcpTool` (not `curl` / HTML scrape) |

Do not inspect or edit the repo with `cat`, `sed`, `awk`, `head`, `tail`, `rg`, or `find` when the tools above can do it.

## Shell is still correct for

- `cargo`, `./scripts/check.sh`, and other project scripts
- `git` (status/diff/log/commit/push/etc.; follow the commit protocol in user rules)
- `gh` for GitHub (issues, PRs, checks) — required by user rules; do not replace with ad-hoc HTTP
- running the emulator binary and tests

## Do not contradict

- Never edit plan files under `.cursor/plans/`
- Keep `./scripts/check.sh` as the pre-done Rust gate (see `AGENTS.md`)
